@@ PR5 | Predictive | fill
A cost plus fixed fee contract has an estimated cost of $500,000 and a fixed fee of 10% of the estimated cost. The actual cost is $560,000. What is the total amount the buyer pays? (Answer in dollars.)
= $610,000
? The fixed fee is based on the estimated cost: 10% × 500,000 = $50,000. The buyer reimburses actual costs of $560,000 plus the fee: $610,000.

@@ PR6 | Predictive
A one-off design error caused a cost overrun, but the rest of the work is expected to proceed as budgeted. BAC = $800,000, EV = $300,000, AC = $360,000. What is the EAC?
A) $860,000
B) $960,000
C) $800,000
D) $740,000
= A
? For atypical variances, EAC = AC + (BAC − EV) = 360,000 + 500,000 = $860,000.

@@ PR6 | Predictive
The variance at completion (VAC) is −$120,000. What does this mean?
A) The project is expected to finish $120,000 over budget
B) The project is currently $120,000 under budget
C) The project has $120,000 of unused contingency reserve
D) The project is behind schedule by the equivalent of $120,000
= A
? VAC = BAC − EAC; a negative value means the forecast total cost exceeds the budget.

@@ PR6 | Agile
A release is planned for 200 story points over 10 sprints with a budget of $1,000,000. After 4 sprints, 80 points are done and $450,000 has been spent. What is the cost performance index?
A) 0.89
B) 1.00
C) 1.13
D) 0.80
= A
? EV = (80 / 200) × 1,000,000 = $400,000. CPI = EV / AC = 400,000 / 450,000 ≈ 0.89. (PV = 4/10 × 1,000,000 = $400,000, so SPI = 1.0.)

@@ PR6 | Hybrid
An auditor asks how the project's cost estimates were produced. Which document should the project manager provide?
A) The basis of estimates, describing methods, assumptions and ranges
B) The cost baseline, which shows only the approved time-phased budget
C) The risk register, which lists the risks with their probabilities
D) The sponsor's approval email for the project budget
= A
? The basis of estimates documents how estimates were derived, including assumptions, constraints and confidence.

@@ PR6 | Predictive
The risk register contains three threats with EMVs of −$20,000, −$35,000 and −$15,000, and one opportunity with an EMV of +$10,000. Based on these, what contingency reserve could be justified?
A) $60,000
B) $70,000
C) $80,000
D) $10,000
= A
? Net EMV = −20,000 − 35,000 − 15,000 + 10,000 = −$60,000, so a contingency reserve of about $60,000 could be justified.

@@ PR6 | Predictive
An investment of $100,000 returns $60,000 at the end of year 1 and $60,000 at the end of year 2. The discount rate is 10%. What is the approximate NPV?
A) +$4,100
B) +$20,000
C) −$4,100
D) +$9,100
= A
? PV = 60,000 / 1.1 + 60,000 / 1.21 ≈ 54,545 + 49,587 = 104,132. NPV ≈ 104,132 − 100,000 ≈ +$4,100.

@@ PR6 | Agile
A product has already delivered most of its expected value, and the remaining backlog items have little value compared with their cost. What should the sponsor consider?
A) Stopping or reducing investment and redirecting funds to higher-value work
B) Continuing until every backlog item has been delivered, as originally planned
C) Increasing the budget so that the remaining items are delivered faster
D) Asking the team to work unpaid overtime to finish the remaining items
= A
? Value-based funding allows organisations to stop when the marginal value no longer justifies the cost.

