@@ PR8 | Predictive
Activity A (5 days) starts the project. Activity B (3 days) and activity C (6 days) both follow A. Activity D (4 days) follows both B and C. What is the early start of activity D?
A) Day 11
B) Day 8
C) Day 15
D) Day 9
= A
? Using a zero-based forward pass: A finishes at day 5; B finishes at 8; C finishes at 11. D starts after the later of B and C, at day 11.

@@ PR8 | Agile
A release burnup shows 240 points of scope, 120 points completed after 6 sprints, and scope growing by 10 points per sprint. If velocity stays at 20 points per sprint, roughly how many more sprints are needed?
A) About 12
B) About 6
C) About 8
D) About 24
= A
? The team gains 20 points per sprint while scope grows by 10, so the gap of 120 points closes by about 10 points per sprint: 120 / 10 = 12 sprints.

@@ PR8 | Predictive
Levelling the concrete surface can begin once pouring has started, without waiting for pouring to finish. Which relationship is this?
A) Start-to-start
B) Finish-to-start
C) Finish-to-finish
D) Start-to-finish
= A
? In a start-to-start relationship, the successor can begin once the predecessor has started.

