A) Leading indicators, such as pilot adoption rates
B) Lagging indicators, such as annual revenue next year
C) The number of meetings held each month
D) The total number of change requests submitted
= A
? Leading indicators predict future outcomes and allow early corrective action.

@@ PR9 | Predictive
A ten-month project has a schedule performance index of 0.80, and the trend is expected to continue. Approximately how long will the project take?
A) About 12.5 months
B) About 8 months
C) About 10 months
D) About 18 months
= A
? A rough forecast is planned duration / SPI = 10 / 0.8 = 12.5 months. (Time-based measures are more precise, but this approximation is common.)

@@ PR9 | Agile
On a cumulative flow diagram, the "Done" band has stayed flat for two weeks, while the other bands keep growing. What does this indicate?
A) Nothing is being completed, so work is piling up
B) The team is working very efficiently and finishing work quickly
C) The scope of the product has decreased over the last two weeks
D) The diagram is not being updated and can therefore be ignored
= A
? A flat Done band means no work is being completed; growing bands show accumulating WIP — a serious flow problem.

@@ PR9 | Agile
The project manager wants a simple indicator of how reliably the team meets its sprint commitments. Which measure is most suitable?
A) The share of sprints in which the sprint goal was met
B) The number of hours that each developer logs in every sprint
C) The number of new stories created by the team in each sprint
D) The average length of each daily scrum during the sprint
= A
? Sprint goal achievement over time shows planning reliability without focusing on individual effort.

@@ PR9 | Predictive | match
Match each earned value measure with its formula.
1) Cost variance
2) Schedule variance
3) Cost performance index
4) Schedule performance index
A) EV − AC
B) EV − PV
C) EV ÷ AC
D) EV ÷ PV
= 1-A, 2-B, 3-C, 4-D
? EV comes first in every variance and index; cost measures use AC and schedule measures use PV.

@@ PR10 | Predictive
At the end of an aircraft modification project, what must be handed over to the customer along with the aircraft?
A) The certification and configuration records needed to operate it
B) The project team's personal notes and emails from the project
C) The draft versions of all the design documents and drawings
D) Only the final invoice and the payment schedule for the project
= A
? Closure includes transferring the documentation the customer needs to operate, maintain and certify the product.

@@ PR10 | Agile
A new system has replaced an old one. Which closure activity is often overlooked?
A) Decommissioning the old system, including data archiving
B) Holding the final sprint review with all stakeholders
C) Updating the product backlog for future enhancements
D) Recognising the team's achievements at a closing event
= A
? Retiring the legacy system — with proper data handling and contract termination — is part of completing the transition.

@@ PR10 | Hybrid
After the festival, what must the project manager complete before closing the project?
A) Settle vendor payments, hand back the venue and capture lessons
B) Start planning next year's festival immediately with the same team
C) Delete all of the vendor contracts from the project records
D) Release the remaining budget without reconciling the final costs
= A
? Closure includes settling contracts and payments, handing back resources such as venues and capturing lessons.

@@ PR10 | Predictive
What is the correct order of these closing activities?
A) Obtain final acceptance, close contracts, capture final lessons, archive records, release the team
B) Release the team, close contracts, obtain final acceptance, archive records, capture lessons
C) Archive records, release the team, obtain final acceptance, close contracts, capture lessons
D) Capture lessons, release the team, archive records, obtain final acceptance, close contracts
= A
? Acceptance comes first, followed by contract and administrative closure, final lessons and archiving, with the team released at the end.

@@ PR10 | Agile
The final release is accepted, and the team will disband. What is a valuable last step?
A) A closing retrospective and recognition of the team's contributions
B) A performance ranking of each team member for their managers
C) A new backlog for a different product the team may build next
D) A list of everyone's mistakes, kept in the archive for reference
= A
? Closing retrospectives capture learning, and recognition honours the team's work before members move on.

@@ PR10 | Predictive | multi
Which two are key outputs of closing a project? (Choose two.)
A) The final product, service or result transition
B) The final report
C) The project charter
D) New change requests for the next project
E) The initial stakeholder register
= A, B
? Closing produces the transition of the final product and the final report, along with updates to organisational assets.
